{
  "_comment": "Launches (SatelliteSimLaunches.cpp; plan .plans/LAUNCHES_PLAN.md). Each program keeps the constellations whose names contain one of its 'match' strings flying: every orbital plane is refreshed once per 'life_years', in launches of 'payload' satellites a 'batch_gap_days' apart. A launch flies from one of its vehicle's sites (one whose latitude and azimuth range reach the plane) at the moment the plane passes over it, deploys a train at 'park_km' that climbs to its slots over 'raise_days', and the satellites it replaces deorbit and re-enter over 'deorbit_days'. A program with a 'crew' block flies a visiting spacecraft to a station (a constellation of one) every 'life_years' (not scaled by the design-life setting): raise_days is lift-off to docking; no train, no retiree. The spacecraft ('model') flies its own phasing, rendezvous and docking, stays docked, undocks and comes home: 'people' (crew) or 'cargo': true; 'lands' (on land, else a splashdown) or 'return': 'burns' (destroyed on re-entry); 'fast_dock_h' = fast-track windows (hours after lift-off); 'ports' = the class of docking port it takes, 'share_crew_ports' = it uses the crews' ports between rotations; 'stay_days' = how long it stays docked; 'heat_shield_m' = its heat shield below the docking port. Vehicle figures are public approximations (2036 is a guess). Sites: azimuth = [min, max] degrees clockwise from north, allowed by range safety (wraps through 360). Pads (drawn on the ground; sites within 150 m share one): optional 'pad_kind' (0 generic, 1 Falcon: service structure + landing zone, 2 Starship: catch tower; default from the vehicles flying there) and 'pad_heading_deg' (default the middle of the azimuth range). Vehicles: 'mount_m' = the launch mount the vehicle stands on, 'catch_m' = how far above it a tower-caught booster stops. Booster recovery at sea (droneships): 'droneship_km' = how far downrange a 'droneship' booster lands (a short trim burn; 0 = where its arc comes down), 'rtls_max_kg' = the heaviest payload with which it flies back to its pad's landing zone instead, 'landing_ships' = [{name, model (data/satellite_models, tools/make_ship_models.py), deck_m (must equal the model's deck), sites (the sites it serves; none = all)}]; a downrange point on land is a ground landing. Programs: 'sat_mass_kg' (per satellite) or 'payload_mass_kg' (the launch's total) picks the recovery.",
